{"id": "EUVD-2026-103698", "enisaUuid": "edc62aea-4102-3dfd-ae81-5455289100b7", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: ISO: release unused CIS holds after channel attach\n\nhci_bind_cis() and hci_connect_cis() return one hci_conn hold for the\nISO layer.  A new channel association consumes that hold, which is\neventually released by iso_conn_free().\n\nThere are two cases where iso_chan_add() does not create an association:\nit returns success when the socket is already attached to the same\niso_conn, and it returns -EBUSY when another socket is attached.  The\nhold returned for the current call is unused in both cases.  This occurs\nwhen deferred setup calls iso_connect_cis() again for its existing\nsocket, or when another socket attempts to reuse the CIS.\n\nDetect the idempotent case while the connection is locked and release\nthe unused hold after iso_chan_add().  Also release it on -EBUSY.  Do not\ndrop it for other errors: a newly allocated iso_conn releases the\ntransferred hold when its last temporary reference is put.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:15:07", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:19:54", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e0e8b70207eaf27aee0a05ec5bf2d1b6bcb004d1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ed4c026cc4094dfb7a329b9d8df0ddd0be1b2458", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e5fcca51177f224604e3a8c926ffd5edbeb58b09", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0fcd4dad555c96e0bd3a1b8c569f989be85c7341"], "aliases": ["GHSA-9rg4-gm9p-59qp", "CVE-2026-98458"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0d0748e8-22c3-3251-943e-a555ce452110", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "33e8da3e-2ea1-3cbd-a9db-42cc67040a5f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "69997d50ec574be816b4ee8f9cee52ebbd53f8bd <e0e8b70207eaf27aee0a05ec5bf2d1b6bcb004d1"}, {"id": "3468c6dd-6438-3c67-ab94-0cc637af3a6b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "3d4d46c1-8318-3083-bd55-78c01561d96d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "69997d50ec574be816b4ee8f9cee52ebbd53f8bd <e5fcca51177f224604e3a8c926ffd5edbeb58b09"}, {"id": "3f0d76ba-6f26-364f-b614-f5fb92ab1947", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "465db7e5-b665-37fa-8f2f-adbad7484d30", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "822458b6-ff36-334d-8efa-205e07960a6e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "69997d50ec574be816b4ee8f9cee52ebbd53f8bd <ed4c026cc4094dfb7a329b9d8df0ddd0be1b2458"}, {"id": "93437702-8ac7-3b81-9b01-42612937ddf9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "69997d50ec574be816b4ee8f9cee52ebbd53f8bd <0fcd4dad555c96e0bd3a1b8c569f989be85c7341"}, {"id": "a83d40c7-0800-3fee-a869-bcc67947258e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "aeae7e9c-bc8c-30c0-a2eb-529c5dc56e78", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7be40f4b-7f68-3e6a-90a0-7a0ab790c469", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}